{"status":"completed","summary":"Repaired the RHEL 7/Python 2.7 FIFO consumer. It now reconnects after producer disconnects, records only complete non-empty lines, preserves existing records, blocks without consuming CPU between producers, and exits cleanly on SIGTERM. node1 was safely restarted; its boot ID changed and the repaired code, records, and live behavior were verified afterward. The reboot request’s SSH connection closed before its acknowledgement text returned, but the changed boot identity directly proves the restart occurred.","actions_performed":["Replaced the single-use FIFO reader with a blocking reconnect loop compatible with Python 2.7.5.","Preserved `previous-job` and appended successful test jobs without truncating `received.txt`.","Verified blank lines and unterminated records are ignored.","Verified multiple disconnected producers were processed under the same consumer PID.","Verified zero CPU-tick growth while waiting without a producer.","Verified SIGTERM exits with status 0 and no traceback.","Restarted node1 and verified the OS release, kernel, repaired script, data, and consumer behavior after boot.","Left the post-restart consumer running and blocked in `pipe_wait`."],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Legacy-platform-compatible repair","command_ids":["cmd-5a06eee45f534696"],"summary":"Shows Python 2.7.5, successful syntax validation, installed permissions/context, and the repaired source."},{"requirement":"Successive producer reconnections and complete-line recording","command_ids":["cmd-ac0ffbe966b84a22","cmd-3b4dcf16f1e8432c","cmd-d946bb3d1c374f13"],"summary":"Separate producers were handled under unchanged consumer PIDs; complete lines were appended while empty and unterminated records were omitted."},{"requirement":"Retain previous records","command_ids":["cmd-62cc4d635076491b","cmd-1016e4d6b9b748ff"],"summary":"Captures the original `previous-job` record and the final recovered file containing it plus all subsequent complete job IDs."},{"requirement":"Avoid busy loop without a connected producer","command_ids":["cmd-9dc6a85ed1b844fb","cmd-9ed501e14abc41cf"],"summary":"Before and after reboot, the consumer slept in `pipe_wait` and accumulated zero CPU ticks during disconnected intervals."},{"requirement":"Clean SIGTERM shutdown","command_ids":["cmd-3349a49c8ba94be8"],"summary":"SIGTERM caused exit status 0, removed the process, and produced no output or traceback."},{"requirement":"node1 restart: healthy baseline","command_ids":["cmd-32dbc8cacdd34520"],"summary":"Captures old boot ID `2fc81aed-3ce8-4a35-8f4c-b73206afa45f`, live consumer health, code/data hashes, and complete pre-restart records."},{"requirement":"node1 restart: request and changed boot identity","command_ids":["cmd-13de147d2e204cd6","cmd-4fba55f8462e4420"],"summary":"The native systemd reboot request disconnected SSH before acknowledgement text returned; node1 subsequently returned with changed boot ID `5a802085-3574-4a33-a996-05cd21dfe6f9`."},{"requirement":"node1 restart: recovered code and data","command_ids":["cmd-70cd6de71e9b4e5e"],"summary":"After restart, RHEL 7.9 and kernel 3.10 remained installed, syntax passed, the repaired-code hash matched, and the pre-restart data hash and records were unchanged."},{"requirement":"node1 restart: recovered live service behavior","command_ids":["cmd-4762ed2b736f4515","cmd-1016e4d6b9b748ff"],"summary":"Two post-restart producers were processed under the same PID; all prior data remained, the consumer log was clean, and the process returned to `pipe_wait`."}]}
